-reference-completeness","usage":{"input_tokens":48307,"output_tokens":2595,"requests":4}}],"version":1},"findings":[{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Extend the sandbox scope (and an enforcement test) to the `mutmut run *mutants` invocation in `_diagnose_non_killed()` (scripts/mutation_gate.py:666), which also executes mutated code on the mainline when a mutant survives, and correct the 'Which subprocess matters' section to account for this fifth subprocess.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.2,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'execute_shard() spawns four subprocesses via _run(). Only two execute shard test code and are in scope'","scripts/mutation_gate.py:665-666: `_run((sys.executable, \"-m\", \"mutmut\", \"run\", *mutants, \"--max-children\", \"1\"), cwd=root, env=env)` — mutated code, no sandbox wrap","scripts/mutation_gate.py:731: `diagnostic = _diagnose_non_killed(head_root, head_run, shard_artifacts)` invoked whenever comparison.failures (a survivor) is present — the incident condition"],"finding":"The plan's subprocess-scoping analysis ('Which subprocess matters') enumerates only the four subprocesses in execute_shard() and concludes only the baseline pytest (579) and mutmut run (583) execute mutated code. It misses _diagnose_non_killed() (scripts/mutation_gate.py:660), which runs on the mainline (called at line 731 whenever a mutant survives) and executes `mutmut run *mutants --max-children 1` at line 666 — re-running MUTATED code, the exact causal path of the 2026-08-26 incident — with NO sandbox (plain _command_env + bare _run, no mutation_sandbox.wrap). The chosen mechanism therefore leaves a live destructive path unsandboxed.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f1c1469db0bd1f8c0","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan section 'Which subprocess matters' / AC1 / scripts/mutation_gate.py:660-669, 731","norm_id":"n906021401ddb5f82","priority":1.0,"reason":"hi